<article class="env-lemma" id="030Q">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/030Q">Lemma <span data-tag="030Q">10.42.3</span>.</a> Let $K/k$ be a separably generated, and finitely generated field extension. Set $r = \text{trdeg}_ k(K)$. Then there exist elements $x_1, \ldots , x_{r + 1}$ of $K$ such that </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$x_1, \ldots , x_ r$ is a transcendence basis of $K$ over $k$, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$K = k(x_1, \ldots , x_{r + 1})$, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$x_{r + 1}$ is separable over $k(x_1, \ldots , x_ r)$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Combine the definition with Fields, Lemma <a href="/tag/030N" data-tag="030N">9.19.1</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>